<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-AAMODT WINS MEN'S COMBINED GOLD.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-AAMODT WINS MEN'S COMBINED GOLD.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Kjetil-Andre Aamodt won the men's combined gold medal at the Alpine skiing world championships in a total time of three minutes 10.40 seconds on Thursday, according to unofficial results.  </p>
<p>Switzerland's Bruno Kernen took the silver in 3:10.68 and Austrian Mario Reiter won bronze in 3:11.69.</p>
